    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p>Criteria for suspected or confirmed hereditary leiomyomatosis and renal cell carcinoma (HLRCC) diagnosis (modified according to {20618355})</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoTableGridLight\" style=\"width: 678.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"1\" width=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 3.5pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 678.9pt; border: solid #BFBFBF 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"905\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"font-weight: normal;\">Clinically, the diagnosis should be suspected if the major criterion or &ge;&nbsp;2&nbsp;minor criteria are fulfilled </span></strong><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{20618355}</span><strong><span style=\"font-weight: normal;\">:</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 70.3pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.95pt; border: solid #BFBFBF 1.0pt; border-top: none; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 70.3pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"19\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"font-weight: normal;\">&nbsp;</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 664.95pt; border-top: none; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid #BFBFBF 1.0pt; border-right: solid #BFBFBF 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 70.3pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"887\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Major criterion</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Multiple, histologically confirmed cutaneous piloleiomyomas</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Minor criteria</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Severely symptomatic uterine leiomyoma before the age of 40&nbsp;years (surgical therapy needed)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Renal cell carcinoma before the age of 40&nbsp;years</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>A first-degree family member fulfilling one of the criteria above</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 3.5pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 678.9pt; border: solid #BFBFBF 1.0pt; border-top: none; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"905\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"font-weight: normal;\">The diagnosis is confirmed if a pathogenic variant of </span></strong><em>FH</em><strong><span style=\"font-weight: normal;\"> is detected or if both of the following criteria are fulfilled </span></strong><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{20301430}</span><strong><span style=\"font-weight: normal;\">:</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 9.7pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.95pt; border: solid #BFBFBF 1.0pt; border-top: none; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 9.7pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"19\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"font-weight: normal;\">&nbsp;</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 664.95pt; border-top: none; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid #BFBFBF 1.0pt; border-right: solid #BFBFBF 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 9.7pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"887\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>&ge;&nbsp;2&nbsp;cutaneous leiomyomas (with &ge;&nbsp;1&nbsp;histologically confirmed) without a family history of HLRCC or<br />&ge;&nbsp;1&nbsp;cutaneous leiomyoma with a family history of HLRCC</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><strong><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; font-weight: normal;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></strong>&ge;&nbsp;1&nbsp;renal cell carcinoma with compatible morphology and immunohistochemistry (with or without a family history of HLRCC)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 36610,
    "bookid": 34,
    "chapterId": 473,
    "fileId": 13464,
    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p>Clinical and pathological findings of tumours associated with hereditary leiomyomatosis and renal cell carcinoma (HLRCC)</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Ramona Erber",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoTableGridLight\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"0\" width=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 3.5pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.85pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"118\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.9pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"175\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Cutaneous leiomyoma</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.15pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Uterine leiomyoma</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 218.15pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"291\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Renal cell carcinoma (RCC)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.25pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"118\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Other tumours</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"118\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Localization</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"175\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Skin <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{15937070}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Uterus <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{15937070}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 218.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"291\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Predominantly in renal cortex <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{17895761}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"118\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.85pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"118\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Clinical features</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"175\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Mean age of onset is 25&nbsp;years; can be solitary or multiple; predominantly involves trunk or extremities; number can increase with time <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{15937070; 12772087}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Occurs in almost 100% of women with HLRCC, at a mean age of 30&nbsp;years (range: 18&ndash;53&nbsp;years); multiple, large, bulky, and highly symptomatic, often resulting in early surgical intervention <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{15937070; 12772087}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 218.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"291\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Affects 14% of HLRCC patients, typically presenting in the fourth or fifth decade of life as a unilateral solitary renal tumour <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{17895761; 12772087; 15937070; 11248088}</span>; often asymptomatic or less frequently presents with back pain, palpable mass, or haematuria <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{20301430}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"118\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"118\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Macroscopic appearance</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"175\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Skin-coloured or light-brown nodules <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{15937070}</span>, 0.4&ndash;2.5&nbsp;cm in size <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{12772087}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Multiple and large (up to 10&nbsp;cm) <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{12772087}</span>; the cut surface is firm, tan to white, and whorled (similar to sporadic leiomyomas)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 218.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"291\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Variable cystic and solid parts; measures 2.3&ndash;22&nbsp;cm <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{17895761; 11248088}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"118\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.85pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"118\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Histopathology</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.9pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"175\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Nodular smooth muscle proliferation growing in interlacing bundles with centrally located blunt-edged nuclei, similar to sporadic tumours <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{11248088}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 177.15pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"236\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Conventional, cellular, or with bizarre nuclei; often displays characteristic features such as staghorn vasculature, alveolar oedema, ovoid nuclei arranged in chains, eosinophilic cytoplasmic inclusions, and nuclei with prominent eosinophilic nucleoli surrounded by haloes; some cases can also display Schwannian-like features <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{29332133; 28664937}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 218.15pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"291\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Can show a variety of growth patterns (papillary, tubular, tubulopapillary, tubulocystic, collecting duct&ndash;like, eosinophilic SDHB-like RCC, and mixed growth <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{11248088; 17895761; 15937070; 12772087; 28165631}</span>), but the characteristic finding is prominent inclusion-like eosinophilic nucleoli surrounded by a perinucleolar halo <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{11248088; 17895761; 15937070; 12772087; 28165631}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.25pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"118\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Rarely, unilateral or bilateral nodular hyperplasia of adrenal gland can occur <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{22982371}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
